   <h3> The Library and Treasury</h3>
   <p>
   
<a href="/index.pl?node=The%20Library&lastnode_id=624">The Library</a> is maintained by Zorbitan (aka <a href="/index.pl?node=Inertia&lastnode_id=624">Inertia</a>).  The goal of
the Library is to provide a repository of words, runes, pages, and other
spell research components for the casters in Bloodhorde.  All members are
strongly encouraged to save all spell research components found and donate
them to the Library so that the casters will have a central place to find
most, if not all, of their research components.

<p><a href="/index.pl?node=The%20Treasury&lastnode_id=624">The Treasury</a> is maintained by Plarg (aka <a href="/index.pl?node=Runja&lastnode_id=624">Runja</a>).  The treasury can
be thought of as a kind of item donation center for the guild.  When you
donate an item to the treasury, you are given credit for that item.  You
can use that credit to "purchase" something else that is in the treasury,
or just leave it as a gift to the guild and help out the younger members.
The credit received is determined by looking up current prices on
different EQ websites.  Significant positive balances for individuals could
lead to promotions within the guild.  Also see <a href="/index.pl?node=The%20Treasury%20FAQ&lastnode_id=624">The Treasury FAQ</a> if you
have questions.

<p>The Bloodhorde also maintains a <a href="/index.pl?node=Quest%20Gem%20Bank&lastnode_id=624">Quest Gem Bank</a> for members to get those elusive quest gems.

<p>Both the Librarian and Treasurer will be logged in at least once a week
(typically on saturday or sunday afternoon).  At that time all members are
encouraged to donate any unused items and any spell components.  If you need
to have access to the Librarian or Treasurer to obtain needed items at times
other than the weekly appearances, you should contact the member responsible
for that duty and set up a time to meet.

